{"vid":"K8Dwy0u5pp8","source":"K8Dwy0u5pp8.en-GB.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"From BBC Learning English,"},{"t":1.7,"txt":"this is Learning English from the News, our podcast about the news headlines."},{"t":6.2,"txt":"In this programme,"},{"t":7.5,"txt":"first solar eclipse in Europe for over 25 years."},{"t":16,"txt":"Hello, I'm Georgie. And I'm Becca."},{"t":18.2,"txt":"In this programme, we look at one big news story"},{"t":21,"txt":"and the vocabulary in the headlines that will help you understand it."},{"t":24.5,"txt":"You can find all the vocabulary and headlines from this episode,"},{"t":28.4,"txt":"as well as a worksheet on our website, bbclearningenglish.com."},{"t":32.9,"txt":"OK, Becca, let's hear more about this story."},{"t":41.4,"txt":"Many parts of Europe will experience a solar eclipse on Wednesday evening."},{"t":46.1,"txt":"A solar eclipse is when the Moon blocks the light from the Sun."},{"t":50.4,"txt":"The Sun will be completely covered for people watching"},{"t":53.2,"txt":"from parts of Spain and Iceland."},{"t":55.7,"txt":"Other parts of Europe will get a partial eclipse."},{"t":58.4,"txt":"For example, in Berlin, 85% of the Sun will be covered."},{"t":62.3,"txt":"92% in Paris and in London 90%."},{"t":66,"txt":"It will be the first solar eclipse in Europe since 1999."},{"t":70.3,"txt":"Wow. Becca, are you going to be watching the eclipse?"},{"t":73.3,"txt":"I am, I'm really excited about it."},{"t":75.8,"txt":"How about you, Georgie?"},{"t":77.1,"txt":"Well, I only heard about it this week, so I don't feel very prepared,"},{"t":81.4,"txt":"but I probably will try and watch it."},{"t":82.9,"txt":"I just need to find a safe way to do it."},{"t":85,"txt":"Yeah, we'll talk more about that a little bit later."},{"t":87.9,"txt":"So, total eclipses are rare events and many people travel to see them."},{"t":92.3,"txt":"And there's going to be a few solar eclipses in the next few years."},{"t":95.8,"txt":"Following the eclipse this summer,"},{"t":97.6,"txt":"there will be a total eclipse in Egypt next August,"},{"t":100.8,"txt":"and a third eclipse in Australia and New Zealand in July 2028."},{"t":105.4,"txt":"And our first headline is about this."},{"t":108.6,"txt":"This headline is from Forbes, a global news organisation."},{"t":112.9,"txt":"A Golden Age Of Total Solar Eclipses Begins Tomorrow."},{"t":116.7,"txt":"And that headline again, A Golden Age Of Total Solar Eclipses Begins Tomorrow,"},{"t":121.9,"txt":"and that's from Forbes."},{"t":124,"txt":"This headline is about this week's solar eclipse and the eclipses"},{"t":127.8,"txt":"that will happen around the world over the next couple of years."},{"t":131.8,"txt":"Yes, the headline says there will be a golden age of total solar eclipses."},{"t":136.7,"txt":"And we are looking at this expression a golden age."},{"t":140,"txt":"Becca, what can you tell us?"},{"t":141.4,"txt":"Well, a golden age is a particularly good or successful period of time."},{"t":146.5,"txt":"Yes. Golden describes the colour of gold, the precious metal."},{"t":150.6,"txt":"We use golden metaphorically to mean something is very good and valuable."},{"t":154.5,"txt":"For example, a golden opportunity."},{"t":157,"txt":"You might hear the expression golden age used to talk about the past."},{"t":161.7,"txt":"For example, we could describe the 1800s as a golden age for manufacturing."},{"t":167.3,"txt":"Or we could talk about the golden age of the internet"},{"t":170.3,"txt":"at the end of the 20th century,"},{"t":172,"txt":"when new technology was developing. With the expression golden age,"},{"t":176.8,"txt":"there's a sense that the period of time we're referring to is rare"},{"t":180.4,"txt":"and will not be repeated, that it's a particularly special time."},{"t":184.3,"txt":"Yes. To return to our headline,"},{"t":186.2,"txt":"it says a golden age of solar eclipses is beginning."},{"t":190,"txt":"This is because there will be three total eclipses over the coming years"},{"t":194.4,"txt":"for people around the world to experience, and it isn't common"},{"t":198.2,"txt":"to get so many opportunities to witness this spectacular event."},{"t":202.2,"txt":"Becca, we could have an extra meaning here,"},{"t":204.1,"txt":"because golden could be describing the light from the Sun as well."},{"t":207.6,"txt":"Ooh. That's true."},{"t":212,"txt":"We've had golden age,"},{"t":213.6,"txt":"a particularly good or successful period of time."},{"t":220.4,"txt":"For example, scientists say that we are in a golden age for cancer treatment."},{"t":225.2,"txt":"New medicines are being discovered all the time."},{"t":230.8,"txt":"This is Learning English from the News, our podcast about the news headlines."},{"t":235.2,"txt":"Today, we're talking about Europe's first solar eclipse since 1999."},{"t":240.2,"txt":"As we mentioned,"},{"t":241.5,"txt":"one of the best places to see the solar eclipse will be in northern Spain,"},{"t":246,"txt":"where the Sun will be completely covered by the Moon."},{"t":248.7,"txt":"Depending on the location,"},{"t":250.3,"txt":"the peak of the total eclipse will be around 8:30 PM"},{"t":254,"txt":"local time."},{"t":255.4,"txt":"Many people are travelling to Spain to experience the eclipse."},{"t":259.2,"txt":"Spanish authorities estimate"},{"t":261.1,"txt":"about 1.5 million additional car journeys will be made in the region."},{"t":266,"txt":"And our next headline is about this."},{"t":268.2,"txt":"This one is from The Guardian, a British newspaper."},{"t":271.6,"txt":"People flocking to Spain to view solar eclipse"},{"t":274.4,"txt":"could spark more 'devastating' wildfires."},{"t":277.6,"txt":"And that headline, again from The Guardian."},{"t":280,"txt":"People flocking to Spain to view solar eclipse"},{"t":282.8,"txt":"could spark more 'devastating' wildfires."},{"t":285.9,"txt":"This article discusses fears about wildfires in the areas of Spain"},{"t":290,"txt":"with the best views of the eclipse."},{"t":292.2,"txt":"We're interested in this word flocking from the headline, Becca."},{"t":295.8,"txt":"Yes, the verb flock means lots of people travel to the same place"},{"t":300,"txt":"at the same time."},{"t":301.4,"txt":"It comes from the noun flock, which means a large group"},{"t":304.5,"txt":"of animals such as sheep or birds."},{"t":307.2,"txt":"In this story, many people will be travelling to northern Spain"},{"t":310.7,"txt":"because of the eclipse, they will be flocking to northern Spain."},{"t":314.8,"txt":"Flock is quite commonly used in news stories about crowds."},{"t":319.2,"txt":"For example, in a heatwave"},{"t":321.5,"txt":"people might flock to the beach, or shoppers"},{"t":324.8,"txt":"might flock to a particular store if there's a sale on."},{"t":328.6,"txt":"We tend to use flock to talk about going to places because people want to."},{"t":333.5,"txt":"It has a sense of excitement."},{"t":335.4,"txt":"We don't use it to talk about leaving places."},{"t":338,"txt":"So you wouldn't normally say people flocked away from something."},{"t":345.6,"txt":"We've had flock, travel in large numbers to a place."},{"t":352,"txt":"For example, crowds flocked to the town centre to watch the parade."},{"t":358.4,"txt":"This is Learning English from the News from BBC Learning English."},{"t":362.4,"txt":"We're talking about the first solar eclipse in Europe in over 25 years."},{"t":367.5,"txt":"So, we know lots of people will be watching the solar eclipse,"},{"t":370.9,"txt":"but you can't actually watch it, right, Becca? Right."},{"t":374.6,"txt":"Looking directly at the sun can damage your eyes, even during an eclipse."},{"t":380.6,"txt":"You can wear special eclipse glasses, which block out most of the light"},{"t":384.6,"txt":"so you can look at the sun safely."},{"t":386.9,"txt":"Or experts say you can make something called a pinhole projector,"},{"t":391.4,"txt":"using paper or cardboard to see how the light changes"},{"t":394.9,"txt":"during the eclipse. Ahead of the solar eclipse,"},{"t":397.8,"txt":"lots of people have been buying eclipse glasses to get the best view"},{"t":401.2,"txt":"of the event, but experts say people should check they are safe to use."},{"t":405.6,"txt":"Let's have another headline."},{"t":407.7,"txt":"This headline is from British radio station LBC."},{"t":412.2,"txt":"'Knock-off' eclipse glasses could cause blindness,"},{"t":415.9,"txt":"experts warn before 'significant' solar event."},{"t":419.1,"txt":"And that headline again from LBC. 'Knock-off' eclipse glasses"},{"t":423.4,"txt":"could cause blindness, experts warn before 'significant' solar event."},{"t":428.3,"txt":"This headline is about the glasses being sold"},{"t":431.2,"txt":"to help people watch the solar eclipse."},{"t":434,"txt":"We're interested in this word knock-off."},{"t":437,"txt":"Yes, a knock-off item is a fake item."},{"t":441.2,"txt":"In this story, experts are warning"},{"t":443.8,"txt":"about knock-off eclipse glasses that could cause blindness."},{"t":447.9,"txt":"These are glasses being sold which claim to be safe to use during the eclipse,"},{"t":452.8,"txt":"but they are fake and won't protect people's eyes properly."},{"t":456.5,"txt":"Knock-off products usually closely resemble the real thing,"},{"t":459.8,"txt":"but are much cheaper because they're poorer quality. Yes."},{"t":464,"txt":"For example, knock-off designer clothes might look like expensive brands,"},{"t":468.6,"txt":"but they're fake and made more cheaply."},{"t":471.3,"txt":"We can use the noun, a knockoff. For example,"},{"t":474.1,"txt":"that t-shirt is a knockoff."},{"t":475.6,"txt":"Or, like in the headline, we can use it as an adjective."},{"t":479.4,"txt":"For example, I saw an advert online for some knock-off trainers,"},{"t":483.1,"txt":"but I didn't buy them as the reviews were all terrible."},{"t":486.5,"txt":"Another word you might see to describe fake products,"},{"t":489.8,"txt":"which closely resembles something more expensive, is dupe."},{"t":494.1,"txt":"So we could say the cheap eclipse glasses are a dupe of the real thing."},{"t":501,"txt":"We've had knock-off, fake."},{"t":505.3,"txt":"For example, my friend bought some knock-off t-shirts online,"},{"t":509,"txt":"but when they arrived, they were terrible quality."},{"t":513,"txt":"Well, that's it for this episode,"},{"t":514.7,"txt":"Becca. If you're in Europe, we hope that you enjoy the solar eclipse,"},{"t":518,"txt":"but remember to stay safe."},{"t":519.6,"txt":"Don't look directly at the sun. Thanks, Georgie."},{"t":522.6,"txt":"I'll definitely be making a pinhole projector."},{"t":526,"txt":"And if you do manage to see the solar eclipse, why not email us"},{"t":529.5,"txt":"about your experience?"},{"t":531,"txt":"Our email address is learningenglish@bbc.co.uk."},{"t":536.3,"txt":"We look forward to hearing from you."},{"t":538,"txt":"Goodbye for now. Bye."}],"words":[{"t":0,"w":"From"},{"t":0,"w":"BBC"},{"t":0,"w":"Learning"},{"t":0,"w":"English,"},{"t":1.68,"w":"this"},{"t":1.68,"w":"is"},{"t":1.68,"w":"Learning"},{"t":1.68,"w":"English"},{"t":1.68,"w":"from"},{"t":1.68,"w":"the"},{"t":1.68,"w":"News,"},{"t":1.68,"w":"our"},{"t":1.68,"w":"podcast"},{"t":1.68,"w":"about"},{"t":1.68,"w":"the"},{"t":1.68,"w":"news"},{"t":1.68,"w":"headlines."},{"t":6.16,"w":"In"},{"t":6.16,"w":"this"},{"t":6.16,"w":"programme,"},{"t":7.48,"w":"first"},{"t":7.48,"w":"solar"},{"t":7.48,"w":"eclipse"},{"t":7.48,"w":"in"},{"t":7.48,"w":"Europe"},{"t":7.48,"w":"for"},{"t":7.48,"w":"over"},{"t":7.48,"w":"25"},{"t":7.48,"w":"years."},{"t":16,"w":"Hello,"},{"t":16,"w":"I'm"},{"t":16,"w":"Georgie."},{"t":16,"w":"And"},{"t":16,"w":"I'm"},{"t":16,"w":"Becca."},{"t":18.24,"w":"In"},{"t":18.24,"w":"this"},{"t":18.24,"w":"programme,"},{"t":18.24,"w":"we"},{"t":18.24,"w":"look"},{"t":18.24,"w":"at"},{"t":18.24,"w":"one"},{"t":18.24,"w":"big"},{"t":18.24,"w":"news"},{"t":18.24,"w":"story"},{"t":21,"w":"and"},{"t":21,"w":"the"},{"t":21,"w":"vocabulary"},{"t":21,"w":"in"},{"t":2